====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|dated}} A path, carriage-way, or road through a park or a landscaped [[right of way]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Garden and Forest: A Journal of Horticulture, Landscape Art | editor=Charles Sprague Sargent| year=1897| page=409| title=The Advertising Nuisance [Editorial Article]| passage=In the case of offensive advertising in the neighborhood of a '''parkway''', it is evident that such advertising is displayed to attract the attention of the people that frequent a public pleasure-ground.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Documents| publisher=Boston (Mass.)| title=Annual Report of the Park Department for the Year 1896| year=1897| passage=As this scheme cannot be carried out without further legislation, application will have to be made to the General Court for authority to construct a way which will serve the purposes of a '''parkway''' and for ordinary travel.}}
# {{rfv-sense|en}} A [[road]]; a [[thoroughfare]].
# {{lb|en|US}} A [[scenic]] [[freeway]].
# {{lb|en|US}} A [[divided highway]] with a [[landscaped]] [[median]].
# {{lb|en|Chicago}} A [[tree lawn]].

